## 15. Import Requirements

### v0 Import Strategy

For same-day MVP, wardOS should support one of the following:

- Manual CSV import from Google Sheet tabs
- Manual copy/paste import
- Seed script from exported CSV files
- Hardcoded sample data based on current known tabs

### v1 Import Strategy

Later versions should support:

- Google OAuth
- Read selected Google Sheets
- Read selected Google Calendar
- Read selected Google Drive folder
- Import review before saving records
- Source links back to original docs/sheets/events

### Import Review

wardOS should not blindly import all extracted data.

Import candidates should have statuses:

- Pending review
- Approved
- Ignored
- Marked sensitive
- Needs editing

Import review should allow the user to:

- Approve item
- Edit item
- Ignore item
- Mark source as sensitive
- Link back to original source

## 16. Privacy Requirements

wardOS must include privacy guardrails from the start.

### Privacy Rules

- Do not store official membership records.
- Do not store confidential pastoral notes.
- Do not store worthiness, financial, counseling, or family-sensitive information.
- Do not automatically summarize sensitive tabs.
- Do not expose internal data through public links.
- Public signup forms should only collect what is necessary.
- Public Sunday program should only display intentionally published content.
- Sensitive Google Sheet tabs should be excluded from default import.
- Users should be able to delete imported data.

### Sensitive Source Handling

For tabs or documents marked sensitive:

- Do not import row-level data.
- Do not summarize with AI.
- Do not show content on the dashboard.
- Store only source title and link if needed.
- Require intentional user action to import any field.

